# Paths: who owns what

Stay inside your area. Every PR keeps its area's section of HANDOFF.md
current and ends with the HANDOFF block.

| Area | Paths | Branch prefix | Primary | Backup |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Contract | `contract/`, `.cursor/rules/` | `contract/*` | Joe in Cursor | Devin |
| Data | `data/` | `devin/data-*` (backup `cursor-data/*`) | Devin | Cursor cloud agent (data) |
| Integration and review | PR reviews, merge list | n/a | Devin (Devin Review) | Codex review; the Wringer adds an adversarial pass |
| Engines | `engines/` | `claude/engines-*` | Claude Code | Devin |
| Eval and CI | `eval/`, `.github/workflows/` | `codex/eval-*` | Codex | Claude Code |
| Web | `web/` | `cursor-web/*` | Cursor cloud agents | Codex |
| Docs | `docs/` | `desk/docs-*` | Hackathon Desk docs seat (Grok Bot) | Claude Code |
| Front matter and ops | `README.md`, `metadata.json`, `DECLARED_PREEXISTING.md`, `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, `ops/` | `desk/ops-*` | Hackathon Desk (Grok Bot) | Devin |
| Deck, script, explanation | `ops/narrative/` | `desk/ops-*` | Hackathon Desk (Grok Bot) | Claude Code |

Contract changes go in their own PR on a `contract/*` branch. Joe presses
merge at the merge windows, about 1 PM and 10 PM ET, in the order data,
engines, eval, web, docs.
